    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Vestaburg is an unincorporated community in Washington County, Pennsylvania, located along PA Route 88 and the Monongahela River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vestaburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around the Vesta Coal Company, a Jones & Laughlin subsidiary, with the Vesta No. 5 mine opening in 1908 and producing coal at a world‑record rate by 1918.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vestaburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Vestaburg in 1916, marking the community’s rise alongside the booming bituminous coal industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vestaburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Vestaburg sits on a compact 0.191 square‑mile area, bordered by the Monongahela River to the east and Fayette County across the waterway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vestaburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The landscape features undulating hills and floodplain along the Monongahela, giving the area a rugged yet scenic character typical of southwestern Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vestaburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Climate in Vestaburg follows a humid continental zone, with cold winters averaging 22°F lows and warm summers reaching 82°F highs.",
